<section class="block" id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="pb_h2">Bad clips are expensive twice</h2>
    <div class="why">
      <div><h3 data-i18n="pb1_t">You pay to collect them</h3><p data-i18n="pb1_d">Operators, contributors and robot time are paid for every hour recorded, usable or not.</p></div>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="pb2_t">Then they hurt the model</h3><p data-i18n="pb2_d">A dark, shaky or incomplete demonstration teaches the robot the wrong thing. Teams that filter their data get better results from fewer hours.</p></div>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="pb3_t">Watching it all doesn't scale</h3><p data-i18n="pb3_d">Reviewing hours of footage by eye is slow and inconsistent. Quality control becomes the bottleneck of the whole data pipeline.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block alt" id="product">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="ck_h2">What HUMI checks</h2>
    <ul class="checks-grid">
      <li><i class="k-dark"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck1_t">Light</h3><p data-i18n="ck1_d">Too dark or overexposed, for the whole clip or just a few seconds.</p></div></li>
      <li><i class="k-blur"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck2_t">Sharpness</h3><p data-i18n="ck2_d">Out-of-focus or smudged footage, ignoring ordinary motion blur from fast hands.</p></div></li>
      <li><i class="k-shake"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck3_t">Camera shake</h3><p data-i18n="ck3_d">Sustained shaking of a head- or chest-mounted camera.</p></div></li>
      <li><i class="k-hand"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck4_t">Hands in frame</h3><p data-i18n="ck4_d">How long one or both hands are visible, and when they leave the picture.</p></div></li>
      <li><i class="k-face"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck5_t">Faces and privacy</h3><p data-i18n="ck5_d">Flags clips where a face appears, before they reach a customer or a model.</p></div></li>
      <li><i class="k-basic"></i><div><h3 data-i18n="ck6_t">File basics</h3><p data-i18n="ck6_d">Length, resolution, frame rate and unreadable files.</p></div></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="parts-note"><strong data-i18n="ck_next_t">In development:</strong> <span data-i18n="ck_next_d">task pace, frozen frames, duplicate clips and sensor timing for teleoperation logs.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="how_h2">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><span class="n">1</span><h3 data-i18n="s1_t">Install it on your side</h3><p data-i18n="s1_d">HUMI runs on your own computers or servers. Nothing is uploaded to us.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n">2</span><h3 data-i18n="s2_t">Point it at a batch</h3><p data-i18n="s2_d">Drop in a folder of clips. Each one is measured once, a few times per second.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n">3</span><h3 data-i18n="s3_t">Set your own limits</h3><p data-i18n="s3_d">Sliders and presets decide what counts as too dark, too blurry or too shaky. Verdicts update instantly.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n">4</span><h3 data-i18n="s4_t">Act on the report</h3><p data-i18n="s4_d">Pay for usable clips, send rejects back with the reason, keep the good sections. Export to CSV or JSON.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block alt" id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="why_h2">Why HUMI</h2>
    <div class="why">
      <div><h3 data-i18n="w1_t">Your data stays in Japan</h3><p data-i18n="w1_d">Robot training video is often confidential. HUMI runs where your data already is, so there is nothing to upload and nothing to approve.</p></div>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="w2_t">Your rules, not ours</h3><p data-i18n="w2_d">Every buyer has different standards. You set the limits for each check and save them as your own preset.</p></div>
      <div><h3 data-i18n="w3_t">Built from the factory floor</h3><p data-i18n="w3_d">Made by an engineer from manufacturing and machine vision, with support in Japanese, English and French.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block quote" id="pilot">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <h2 data-i18n="pl_h2">Request a pilot</h2>
      <p class="sub" data-i18n="pl_p">We're working with a small number of data-collection teams, robot makers and labs in Japan. Tell us about your data and we'll run HUMI on a sample batch with you.</p>
      <p class="alt-mail"><span data-i18n="form_alt">Prefer email? Write to</span> <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
    </div>
    <form class="full" id="pilot-form" action="{{ site.formEndpoint }}" method="POST">
      <div><label for="f-name" data-i18n="f_name">Name</label><input id="f-name" name="name" autocomplete="name" required></div>
      <div><label for="f-company" data-i18n="f_company">Company or lab</label><input id="f-company" name="company" autocomplete="organization" required></div>
      <div class="wide"><label for="f-email" data-i18n="f_email">Work email</label><input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></div>
      <div><label for="f-type" data-i18n="f_type">Type of data</label>
        <select id="f-type" name="data_type">
          <option value="egocentric" data-i18n="o_ego">First-person (egocentric) video</option>
          <option value="teleop" data-i18n="o_teleop">Teleoperation / robot camera</option>
          <option value="umi" data-i18n="o_umi">Handheld gripper (UMI-style)</option>
          <option value="other" data-i18n="o_other">Other or mixed</option>
        </select></div>
      <div><label for="f-hours" data-i18n="f_hours">Hours collected per month</label>
        <select id="f-hours" name="hours_per_month">
          <option value="<100" data-i18n="o_h1">Under 100</option>
          <option value="100-1000" data-i18n="o_h2">100 to 1,000</option>
          <option value=">1000" data-i18n="o_h3">More than 1,000</option>
          <option value="unknown" data-i18n="o_h4">Not sure yet</option>
        </select></div>
      <div class="wide"><label for="f-notes" data-i18n="f_notes">How do you check quality today? (optional)</label><textarea id="f-notes" name="notes" style="min-height:100px"></textarea></div>
      <input type="hidden" name="form" value="pilot">
      <input type="hidden" name="language" id="f-lang" value="en">
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
      <label class="check wide"><input type="checkbox" required> <span><span data-i18n="f_consent">I agree to the</span> <a href="#privacy" data-i18n="f_privacy">privacy policy</a>.</span></label>
      <div class="wide"><button class="btn" type="submit" data-i18n="f_submit">Request a pilot</button></div>
      <p class="status" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block alt" id="research">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="rs_h2">Research</h2>
    <p class="sub-lead" data-i18n="rs_p">We track Japan's robotics and physical-AI supply chain with public data, and write about what it means for the people building robots.</p>
    {% set enPosts = collections.posts %}
    {% if enPosts.length %}
    <ul class="posts">
      {% for post in enPosts | head(3) %}
      <li><a href="{{ post.url }}">
        <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>
        <div><h2>{{ post.data.title }}</h2>{% if post.data.description %}<p>{{ post.data.description }}</p>{% endif %}</div>
      </a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    <p class="parts-note"><a href="/blog/" data-i18n="art_all">All articles</a> · <a href="/ja/blog/" lang="ja">日本語の記事</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block faq" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 data-i18n="faq_h2">Questions</h2>
    <details><summary data-i18n="q1">Is our video uploaded anywhere?</summary><p data-i18n="a1">No. HUMI is installed on your own machines and processes video there. We never receive your footage unless you choose to share a sample with us.</p></details>
    <details><summary data-i18n="q2">Which formats does it read?</summary><p data-i18n="a2">MP4, MOV, AVI, MKV and WEBM video today. Support for robot logs (MCAP, LeRobot) is in development.</p></details>
    <details><summary data-i18n="q3">Can it tell whether the task was done correctly?</summary><p data-i18n="a3">Not yet. Today it checks whether the footage is usable: light, sharpness, shake, hands and privacy. Task-level checks are on our roadmap, starting with assembly and handling tasks.</p></details>
    <details><summary data-i18n="q4">What does it cost?</summary><p data-i18n="a4">Pilots with early partners are free. After that, a flat yearly license per company with unlimited use, updates and support included.</p></details>
    <details><summary data-i18n="q5">Who is it for?</summary><p data-i18n="a5">Teams that collect or buy robot training data in Japan: data-collection companies, humanoid and robot makers, and research labs.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

